# Line endings are normalised to LF in the working tree, not just in the object
# store.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true checks these files out with CRLF on Windows
# while git stores LF — so `npm run build:plugin` hashed different bytes
# depending on who ran it. Three builds of identical source produced three
# different archives, which made the committed .sha256 unverifiable and meant a
# rebuild could offer every client site an "update" containing byte-identical
# code. build-plugin.js documents itself as byte-reproducible; this is what
# makes that true.
#
# It also removes a whole class of test bug: an assertion matching on "\n"
# passed for whoever wrote the file and failed on a fresh clone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never touches the bytes.
*.zip  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
